# CVE-2026-11822 / CVE-2026-11824 — sqlite-libs (RHEL 9.8 base image of Dockerfile_keycloak ->
# quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.6.4) (HIGH). Not exploitable here: Keycloak connects to MSSQL
# (KC_DB: mssql in docker-compose.yml), not sqlite, and has no JNI bindings calling into the
# native sqlite-libs RPM; the FTS5/heap-overflow attack path requires an app that invokes
# SQLite's engine directly. The repo's only sqlite reference is the npm better-sqlite3
